# Copy to mailhawk.env (do not commit).

# --- ARC discovery (prefer env override) ---
# Sibling layout:
#   Projects\MailHawk
#   Projects\arc          <- contains pm.ps1
# ARC_PATH=C:\Users\YOU\Projects\arc

# --- Optional managed environment tokens (never commit a populated file) ---
# Prefer ARC or Configuration > Credentials > Manual (session only).
# Manual tokens submitted through the GUI are NEVER written into this file.
# Only use token environment settings if authorized by your workstation policy.
# GenAi  (api.genai.mil)              -> GENAI_TOKEN      + ARC service genapi
# Grok   (Advana Databricks / Jupiter)-> DATABRICKS_TOKEN + ARC service advana-api
# GENAI_TOKEN=
# DATABRICKS_TOKEN=

# --- ARC service name overrides (optional; defaults are canonical) ---
# MAILHAWK_ARC_ITEM_GenAi=genapi
# MAILHAWK_ARC_ITEM_Grok=advana-api
# CASCADE_ARC_ITEM_GenAi=genapi
# CASCADE_ARC_ITEM_Grok=advana-api
# CASCADE_ARC_ITEM_Llm=genapi

# --- Optional LLM overrides ---
# LLM_URL=
# LLM_MODEL=
# MAILHAWK_LLM_PROFILE=Auto          # Auto | Grok | GenAi

# --- Lifecycle ---
# Closing the MailHawk browser tab stops the local PowerShell service (20 s after the last
# heartbeat, never during a scan). Set to 0 to keep it running (same as MailHawk.bat --stay).
# MAILHAWK_AUTO_STOP=1

# --- Outlook ---
# MAILHAWK_MAX_EMAILS=40
# MAILHAWK_BODY_PREVIEW_CHARS=280
# MAILHAWK_PROVIDER=COM

# Credential source can be chosen live in the browser GUI:
#  - ARC / configured environment: existing ARC bridge and env fallback.
#  - Manual: token held in process memory until server stops or user clears it.
# Do not paste a manual token in this template.

# Privacy: raw AI output may include sensitive mail content; not saved by default.
# Only if approved for debugging: MAILHAWK_SAVE_RAW_AI=1
